+## Failed session setup
+
+- If `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, the orchestrator awaits `onError(session, error)` and then `afterSession(session)` before rejecting with the original error, provided those hooks complete normally; neither user-input processing nor a model response takes place ([validated by: reports and cleans up a failed beforeSession before rejecting with the original error](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L7)).
+
+`afterSession` is a cleanup hook even when setup failed, not evidence that a turn started or completed: `beforeSession` may have allocated nothing or only some resources before throwing, and cleanup must tolerate both. No new started flag is supplied; a deployer must track its own allocations to decide what to release. This is the contract required by HALEngine#94; the acceptance test remains red until that change is implemented.
+
